# `derive_noaa` cost that exactly once already: a null `ExitCode` from PowerShell 5.1 meant
# the runner never recorded success, so the guard resurrected a FINISHED job ~48 times a day
# for three weeks, each pass paging 3,139 ListObjects over `series/noaa%3A` before printing
# "to derive: 0". Measured marginal cost $22.50/month, and `billing_guard.py:46`'s
# WARN_R2_A = 400_000/day sits ABOVE the peak it produced (264,454 on 2026-08-28), so nothing
# alarmed and nothing would.
#
# COMPLETION EVIDENCE, independent of the sentinels:
#   derive_statcan   logs/derive_statcan_20260823T020739Z.log
#                    "[8207/8207] ... units: 466,341  put 252,425  skipped 213,916  errors 0"
